What Are Robot Tool Changers?
Robot tool changers are sophisticated mechanical interfaces consisting of two mating parts - a master side mounted to the robot arm and a tool side attached to various end-effectors. These systems facilitate rapid, automated swapping of tools such as grippers, welders, and dispensers while maintaining utility connections (electrical, pneumatic, fluid). By enabling a single robot to perform multiple tasks with different tools, these components have become indispensable in modern automated manufacturing environments where flexibility and efficiency are paramount.

